<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Takelot II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Takelot II was a king of the Libyan period of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the second half of the 9th century BCE, usually placed in the Twenty-second Dynasty. His reign was troubled by civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>: his son, the Crown Prince Osorkon, served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> and fought rebels in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, as recorded in the Chronicle of Prince Osorkon at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnak">Karnak</a>. Rival kings such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedubast-i">Pedubast I</a> divided the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/takelot-ii.jpg" alt="Takelot II" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Richard Lepsius (1810-84) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Relief_Takelot_II_Lepsius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
